1
00:00:00,431 --> 00:00:01,561
(Sheldon:)Here you go.

2
00:00:01,766 --> 00:00:05,726
(Sheldon:)This is now the only lab with glassware
washed by a man with two doctorates...

3
00:00:05,936 --> 00:00:09,276
(Sheldon:)...and a restraining order
signed by Carl Sagan.

4
00:00:10,608 --> 00:00:12,108
Soap spots. Wash them again.

5
00:00:13,110 --> 00:00:16,150
(Sheldon:)You're being ridiculous.
Those are perfectly clean.

6
00:00:16,864 --> 00:00:19,364
(Amy:)This beaker used to contain
cerebrospinal fluid...

7
00:00:19,575 --> 00:00:21,615
(Amy:)...from an elephant
that died of syphilis.

8
00:00:21,827 --> 00:00:24,167
(Amy:)If it's, in fact, perfectly clean,
drink from it.

9
00:00:31,337 --> 00:00:33,717
(Sheldon:)Biologists are mean.

10
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:38,590
(Amy:)Perhaps this task
will be a little bit more up your alley.

11
00:00:38,803 --> 00:00:41,763
(Amy:)I need you to count the bacteria spores
on these petri dishes.

12
00:00:41,972 --> 00:00:44,102
(Sheldon:)There was something wrong
with that detergent.

13
00:00:44,308 --> 00:00:47,268
(Sheldon:)- That was way too bubbly.
- I'm sure it was.

14
00:00:47,478 --> 00:00:50,818
(Sheldon:)I intend to write that soap company
a strongly-worded letter.

15
00:00:51,148 --> 00:00:53,988
(Amy:)Yeah, good for you.
Now start counting.

16
00:00:54,443 --> 00:00:56,073
(Sheldon:)You know what this place needs?

17
00:00:56,278 --> 00:01:00,018
(Sheldon:)A suggestion box.

